  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1254 AM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nLittle overall change is expected through the forecast period as a \nmid-level ridge remains the dominant feature across South Texas. Hot \nand generally rain-free conditions will persist through the next \nweek, with afternoon highs ranging from the 90s across the Coastal \nBend to around 105 degrees over portions of the Rio Grande Plains. \nHeat indices will continue to peak around 110+ degrees at times, \nmaintaining a moderate to major risk of heat-related impacts across \nmuch of the region.\n\nBy the latter half of the week, guidance continues to show a mid to \nupper-level trough progressing eastward across the Midwest and Great \nLakes, with little direct influence expected across South Texas. \nHowever, some model guidance is beginning to indicate the \ndevelopment of a weak inverted trough across the western Gulf and \nDeep South Texas as we head into next weekend. Should this feature \nmaterialize, pockets of deeper moisture could spread over portions \nof the region and lead to increasing rain chances next weekend. \nOverall, ensemble guidance has below normal PWATs preceding this \nweak feature and confidence remains low so very low PoPs are \nwarranted for now. Otherwise, above-normal temperatures and typical \nsummertime southeasterly flow are expected to continue through the \nperiod.",
